course: dictionary
lesson: 14393
title: Being left out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ostracise is a doing word, a verb. It means to leave someone out of a group on purpose and refuse to talk to them or include them. Its forms are ostracise, ostracises, ostracised and ostracising.
explain: «The girls ostracised Priya, so she sat alone and nobody passed her the ball.» The clues are sat alone, nobody passed her the ball and on purpose. Those clues tell you it is about shutting someone out.
explain: Ostracising someone is a form of bullying, and it can really hurt. If someone is left out on purpose again and again, that is serious. Tell a trusted adult.
fact: Ostracise means to leave someone out of a group on purpose.
fact: «Ostracised» is the past tense: «They ostracised him at break yesterday.»
fact: Ostracising someone, shutting them out of games or chats, is a form of bullying that can really hurt.
fact: In ancient Athens, citizens voted with pieces of pottery called ostraka to banish, or ostracise, a citizen from the city.
fact: A good check is to swap in "left out on purpose" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «At break, the others ostracised Ben by turning their backs on him.» What does ostracised mean here? | Asked him to join in | Played a game with him | *Left him out on purpose | Gave him a prize
exercise: Which word is the past tense of ostracise? | ostracising | ostracise | *ostracised | ostracises
exercise: Why is ostracising someone a form of bullying? | It is a game in PE | *It shuts someone out and can really hurt | It means being very tall | It makes new friends
test: «Mo was ostracised from the chat group, so he felt sad and alone.» What does ostracised mean? | Given a new phone | Praised by the teacher | Invited to a party | *Shut out on purpose
test: Which action is ostracising? | Sharing your crisps | Helping someone with their homework | Inviting someone to sit with you | *Refusing to talk to someone and leaving them out
exam: Ostracise means which of these? | To run a race | To paint a picture | *To leave someone out of a group on purpose | To invite someone to join in
